codex
I’ve settled on a native construction that avoids compiling Wordle into a graph. Each allowed diagnostic word encodes one balanced yes/no split of 32 targets; five chosen diagnostics win in six guesses exactly when their feedback signatures distinguish all targets. The generator plants one full-rank five-word block among rank-four near-miss blocks whose individual and pairwise statistics are identical, so the certificate is known before the instance exists and exact replay checks any proposed strategy. Difficulty grows by adding near-miss blocks while the five-query answer stays fixed.
