Step 0 supports a build, but only as Track B. The paper’s Theorem 1 gives exhaustive recursive search in \(|WI|^{O(g)}\), so a constant-guess family cannot honestly claim Track A; at useful sizes that route is still mechanically enormous. I’m testing a native Wordle construction where a planted laminar decision tree is compiled directly into exact Wordle feedback, so the certificate is known without search and remains a genuine strategy tree rather than a graph surrogate.
