+"""Verified generalized-Wordle strategy instances from arXiv:2204.04104.
+
+The solver is given an implicit dictionary in exactly the graph-to-Wordle form
+used by Lemma 4.2 of the paper, with a harmless set of extra tag coordinates.
+A certificate is a short diagnostic spine: five legal guesses whose possible
+feedback histories distinguish every one of 32 latent labels.  The induced
+strategy then wins against every target word in at most six guesses.
+
+Instances are inverse-generated.  One tagged block is sampled as five
+independent balanced cuts; all other blocks are identically distributed at the
+one-query and two-query levels but contain one hidden parity dependence.  The
+planted spine is therefore known before the Wordle instance is assembled.
+Verification never reads that planted answer.
+"""
+
